SebType: which licence covers which part (README.md, "Licences", has the details):

- SebType's own code and files: the MIT licence in LICENSE-SebType, Copyright (c) 2026 S-Sebb. Each folder's
  LICENSE file lists the files in it that are not SebType's own. Those are:
  - android/app/src/main/assets/emoji/emoji.txt: made by data/emoji/ from Unicode's emoji-test.txt and
    Unicode CLDR's annotations, under the Unicode License v3 (android/app/src/main/assets/emoji/LICENSE.txt),
    with SebType's own ASCII faces (data/emoji/ascii.txt).
  - data/en-dict/en_US.dict: AOSP's en_US word list (Apache-2.0) with wordfreq's frequencies under
    CC BY-SA 4.0 (credits below).
  - engines/sebtype-lm/english.gguf: SebType's English model, CC BY-SA 4.0 (credits below).
  - engines/sebtype-lm/chinese.gguf: SebType's Chinese model, CC BY-SA 4.0 (credits below).
  - android/app/src/main/res/font/sebtype_nunito_extrabold.ttf and sebtype_pixelify_semibold.ttf, the fonts in
    art/fonts/, and the glyph outlines in pc/icons/ (Noto Sans CJK and Nunito): the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  - SebType's Mozc in engines/mozc/, pc/linux/mozc-keymap.tsv, and Mozc's Japanese dictionary the Android
    build makes from it (android/app/mozc-dictionary.sh): Mozc's BSD-3-Clause licence and its data's licences.
  - SebType's librime in engines/librime/: librime's BSD-3-Clause.
  - core/src/rime.cpp, which follows fcitx5-rime (Copyright 2017 Xuetian Weng and contributors), and linux/src/tray.h and tray.cpp, ported from Fcitx5's
    notificationitem: LGPL-2.1-or-later (LICENSE-LGPL-2.1).
  - core/src/mozc.cpp, which follows fcitx5-mozc (Mozc's Fcitx 5 frontend, Copyright 2010-2018 Google Inc. and
    2017 Weng Xuetian): Mozc's BSD-3-Clause licence.
  - linux/librime.spec: Fedora's spec, MIT.
  - android/native/src/main/cpp/cmake/: RimeJni's build scripts (MIT) with SebType's changes, under RimeJni's
    licence (android/native/src/main/cpp/cmake/LICENSE).
  - android/gradlew, android/gradlew.bat and android/gradle/wrapper/: Gradle's wrapper, Apache-2.0.
- AOSP LatinIME's decoder in engines/latinime/, unchanged: the Apache License 2.0 (engines/latinime/NOTICE).
- Projects SebType builds or bundles keep their own licences: rime-ice and 白霜 (rime-frost) data GPL-3.0,
  librime, librime-lua and librime-octagram BSD-3-Clause (built into the Linux add-on and the Android app),
  RimeJni MIT, Mozc BSD-3-Clause, llama.cpp MIT. The Windows candidate window takes its layout numbers and
  aqua colours from Weasel (GPL-3.0) as settings, not its code (windows/README.md).

Until #262 (2026-11) the Android app was a modified FUTO Keyboard. The app SebType ships now contains none
of FUTO Keyboard's code or data, only the keyboard service's class name (org.futo.inputmethod.latin.LatinIME,
SebType's own class), kept so an update from that app keeps SebType chosen. Git history keeps the earlier app
under its licence, the FUTO Source First License 1.1.

The Windows setup installs this notice with the licences of the libraries it ships (librime with its plugins
and dependencies, Mozc, llama.cpp, protobuf, OpenCC and the rest) in licenses\ in SebType's folder.

