same licence. Its words come from AOSP LatinIME's en_US word list
(dictionaries/en_US_wordlist.combined.gz, Copyright The Android Open Source Project, Apache-2.0). wordfreq contains data from Google Books Ngrams (http://books.google.com/ngrams), the
Leeds Internet Corpus, Wikipedia, ParaCrawl, OPUS OpenSubtitles 2018 (originally from the OpenSubtitles
project, http://www.opensubtitles.org/), Twitter, and the SUBTLEX word lists by Marc Brysbaert et al.
(http://crr.ugent.be/programs-data/subtitle-frequencies), which are freely available data.

